## Promotion-Oriented Notes

- All source files are structured for direct promotion into a canonical `src/shared/adapters/` tree.
- No demo-only scaffolding; all adapters use real client libraries.
- Integration tests are gated behind infrastructure availability checks — they do not block unit-test CI but provide promotion confidence when infra is present.
- The adapter contract validation module ensures that any future profile addition must satisfy the same completeness and type-safety rules.

## Bounded Gaps

| Gap | Severity | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Redis queue lacks visibility timeout | Low | Sufficient for on-prem contract; Redis Streams upgrade is a future enhancement |
| CloudWatch log sink is single-threaded | Low | Adequate for current scope; buffered writer for high-throughput is future work |
| No SQS/SNS/SecretsManager integration tests | Medium | Would require LocalStack with those services enabled; S3 integration test proves the adapter wiring pattern |
